From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] wlroots: gles2: wait for the GPU when there is no sync timeline

KGSL attaches no implicit fences to dma-bufs, so KMS scanned out unfinished frames (black staircase stripes during animations).
---
--- a/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/render/gles2/pass.c	2026-11-16 01:00:11.021681404 +0400
+++ b/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/render/gles2/pass.c	2026-11-16 01:00:11.053264013 +0400
@@ -57,7 +57,12 @@
 			goto out;
 		}
 	} else {
-		glFlush();
+		/* Without a timeline the buffer goes to KMS relying on implicit
+		 * sync. Qualcomm KGSL (turnip/zink) attaches no implicit fences to
+		 * exported dma-bufs, so the display engine scanned out frames the
+		 * GPU had not finished: black, staircase-shaped bins during
+		 * animations. Wait for the GPU instead. */
+		glFinish();
 	}
 
 	ok = true;
